        <div class="card">
            <h2>What is this?</h2>
            <p>
                If you've noticed network calls to <span class="domain-mention">8-lives-cat.io</span> in your app, 
                don't worry, <span class="highlight">this is expected behavior</span>.
            </p>
            <p>
                This domain hosts RevenueCat's <strong>backup servers</strong>. When our primary infrastructure 
                experiences issues, our SDK automatically and seamlessly switches to these backup servers to keep 
                your app's subscription features running smoothly.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card why-name">
            <h2><span class="icon">✨</span> Why "8 Lives Cat"?</h2>
            <p>
                You know how cats have <a href="#lives-footnote" class="footnote-link">nine lives?*</a> Well, if you're seeing traffic to this domain, 
                it means our primary servers (the cat) have temporarily lost one life.
            </p>
            <p>
                But don't panic, <span class="highlight">there are still 8 lives left</span>! 
                Our backup system is here to keep things running while we sort out any issues with the main servers.
            </p>
            <div class="lives-counter" title="8 lives remaining!">
